<article class="env-lemma" id="04VJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04VJ">Lemma <span data-tag="04VJ">4.27.14</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category and let $S$ be a right multiplicative system of morphisms of $\mathcal{C}$. Let $A, B : X \to Y$ be morphisms of $S^{-1}\mathcal{C}$ which are the equivalence classes of $(f : X' \to Y, s : X' \to X)$ and $(g : X' \to Y, s : X' \to X)$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$A = B$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists a morphism $t : X'' \to X'$ in $S$ with $f \circ t = g \circ t$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists a morphism $a : X'' \to X'$ with $f \circ a = g \circ a$ and $s \circ a \in S$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is dual to Lemma <a href="/tag/04VF" data-tag="04VF">4.27.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>